{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-447599-r4517862","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Okra Plantain Porridge","sourcePageId":447599,"sourceRevision":"4517862","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T03:11:00Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Okra%20Plantain%20Porridge&oldid=4517862","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:09:41.963Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Nigerian recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for porridge","Category:Recipes using catfish","Category:Recipes using chile","Category:Recipes using dryfish","Category:Recipes using fluted pumpkin","Category:Recipes using okra","Category:Recipes using onion","Category:Recipes using palm oil","Category:Recipes using plantain","Category:Recipes using salt","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"4ee315e8fbe187bb0fce6cde3c4ab043cfbf6a716b829614c0e155dd09159962","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Nigerian recipes\n| Servings = 2-3\n| Time = 10-15 minutes\n| Difficulty = 1\n}}\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''Okra plantain porridge''' is a typical Nigerian food prepared from unripe plantain and okra. It is easy to prepare.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*1 unripe [[Cookbook:Plantain|plantain]], peeled and [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Dryfish|dried catfish]], cleaned\n*1 [[Cookbook:Stock Cube|stock cube]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]], [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]]\n*200g [[Cookbook:Palm Oil|palm oil]]\n*100g [[Cookbook:Okra|okra]], [[Cookbook:Grating|grated]]\n*20g [[Cookbook:Fluted Pumpkin|ugu]] leaves, rinsed and [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n*¼ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*1 tablespoon chile-tomato purée (see note)\n\n==Procedure==\n#Combine the plantain and water in a saucepan. Bring to a boil, then simmer for 3–5 minutes.\n#Add the catfish, stock cube, onions, palm oil, okra, and ugu leaves. Stir until a porridge is formed, then cook for an additional 5 minutes.\n#Season with the salt and chile-tomato. Serve hot.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* The chile-tomato purée is a product commonly available in Nigerian supermarkets. It consists of puréed tomato and chile pepper, sometimes with onion and/or red bell pepper added. It may also be called something like \"tomato stew mix\", \"tomato mix\", \"tomato and pepper mix\", or ''ata lilo''. You can make it yourself at home by puréeing the ingredients together and simmering to reduce it slightly, though you will have to determine the ratios yourself. One place to start is 40% tomato + 30% bell pepper + 20% onion + 10% scotch bonnet chile,<ref>{{Citation |last=Lovemrskush |title=Tomato Pepper Mix for Stews and Jollof Rice |date=2021-03-22 |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lhHBuKS1ntI |access-date=2024-09-16}}</ref> but other recipes do exist.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Osinkolu |first=Lola |date=2015-01-07 |title=How to make a starter sauce (Ata lilo) |url=https://cheflolaskitchen.com/starter-sauce-ata-lilo/ |access-date=2024-09-16 |website=Chef Lola's Kitchen |language=en-US}}</ref>\n\n== References ==\n[[Category:Nigerian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for porridge]]\n[[Category:Recipes using plantain]]\n[[Category:Recipes using 